 35NE  Q 24430     CA -2370  CA 29480  CA              2019MO01                 
 35NE cQ $S(2n)=-470 (2019Mo01, FRDM)                                           
 35NE c  2019Ah07: {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X) using a 345-MeV/nucleon, 450-pnA {+48}Ca   
 35NE2c  beam provided by the cascade operation of the RIBF accelerator complex 
 35NE3c  at RIKEN and impinging on a 20-mm-thick beryllium target. Projectile   
 35NE4c  fragments were separated and identified using |DE-tof-B|r by the       
 35NE5c  large-acceptance two-stage separator BigRIPS. Tof was measured using   
 35NE6c  two thin plastic scintillators placed at the intermediate and final    
 35NE7c  foci of the second stage of BigRIPS. B|r was measured from position    
 35NE8c  measurement at the intermediate focus using the plastic scintillator.  
 35NE9c  |DE was measured using a stack of six silicon detectors installed at   
 35NEAc  the final focus. Optimum settings of B|r were tuned to transmit {+33}F 
 35NEBc  for 14 hours and {+36}Ne+{+39}Na for 7.8 hours. The Be target was      
 35NECc  irradiated with 1.4|*10{+17} and 7.8|*10{+16} {+48}Ca ions,            
 35NEDc  respectively. Measured Z vs A/Z particle-identification plot. No       
 35NEEc  {+35}Ne events were observed in either setting. Under {+33}F setting,  
 35NEFc  the expected {+35}Ne yields obtained from LISE++ are 177 {I53} using   
 35NEGc  the production |s=37.8 fb from EPAX 2.15 systematics and 69 {I17} using
 35NEHc  the production |s=14.8 fb {I36} from Q{-g} systematics.                
 35NE c  2022Ah02: Same experimental setup as 2019Ah07 with 540-pnA {+48}Ca     
 35NE2c  beam. Optimum settings of B|r were tuned to transmit {+39}Na for 46.1  
 35NE3c  hours and {+36}Ne for 25.3 hours. Measured Z vs A/Z                    
 35NE4c  particle-identification plot. No {+35}Ne events were observed in either
 35NE5c  setting. Also see 2025Ku15.                                            
 35NE c  2023Ra22: Relativistic Hartree-Bogoliubov model with nuclear energy    
 35NE2c  density functional (EDF) calculations of binding energies.             
 35NE c  2020Mi15: VS-IMSRG ab initio calculations of ground-state energies and 
 35NE2c  S(2n).                                                                 
