 35NA c  2014Do05: A 345-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam was accelerated by the
 35NA2c  superconducting ring cyclotron (SRC) at RIKEN. A 236-MeV/nucleon       
 35NA3c  {+36}Mg secondary beam was produced by the fragmentation of {+48}Ca on 
 35NA4c  a Be target and separated by the BigRIPS separator using the           
 35NA5c  B|r-|DE-B|r method. The secondary reaction targets were 2.54 g/cm{+2}  
 35NA6c  thick carbon and 2.13 g/cm{+2} thick CH{-2} polyethylene. The secondary
 35NA7c  reaction products were identified by the magnetic spectrometer         
 35NA8c  ZeroDegree using the B|r-|DE-B|r method. |g rays in coincidence with   
 35NA9c  {+35}Na were detected using the DALI2 array of 186 large NaI(Tl)       
 35NAAc  detectors. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g, and |g|g-coin.   
 35NABc  Deduced levels, J, |p, and bands. Compared with shell-model            
 35NACc  calculations using the SPDF-M effective interaction.                   
