 35MG4cG excitation energy. 2017Mo26 states that the difference of the |g-ray   
 35MG5cG emission between 1n-knockout and 1p1n-removal reaction channels        
 35MG6cG suggests that the 621 and 670-keV |g rays were emitted from two        
 35MG7cG different excited states. Another possible placement of the 621 and    
 35MG8cG 670-keV |g rays: 2011Ga15 states that it might be possible that the two
 35MG9cG transitions originate from the same level and that their energy        
 35MGAcG difference of 49(11) keV corresponds to the energy spacing of the      
 35MGBcG alleged (5/2-,3/2-) doublet near the ground state. In Adopted Gammas,  
 35MGCcG all |g rays in this dataset are placed to feed the same final levels   
 35MGDcG based on suggestions by 2017Mo26                                       
