 35MG c  2017Mo26: A secondary beam composed of {+36}Mg and {+37}Al was produced
 35MG2c  via the projectile fragmentation of a 345-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary  
 35MG3c  beam impinging on a {+9}Be target and selected by the BigRIPS separator
 35MG4c  at RIKEN. E({+36}Mg)=235 MeV/nucleon and E({+37}Al)=246 MeV/nucleon in 
 35MG5c  front of the 2.54 g/cm{+2} carbon secondary target. The reactions      
 35MG6c  leading to {+35}Mg from {+36}Mg and {+37}Al are likely 1n-knockout and 
 35MG7c  1p1n-removal reactions, respectively. The reaction residues were       
 35MG8c  selected and identified by the Zero Degree spectrometer using the      
 35MG9c  B|r-|DE-ToF method. The |g rays in coincidence with {+35}Mg residues   
 35MGAc  were detected using the DALI2 array of 186 NaI(Tl) crystals at         
 35MGBc  20|'-150|'. Measured E|g(>200 keV), I|g, ({+35}Mg)|g-coin, the         
 35MGCc  inclusive one-neutron knockout cross section and exclusive |g-ray      
 35MGDc  emission cross sections, and parallel momentum distributions of {+35}Mg
 35MGEc  in coincidence with |g rays. Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, and |p.   
 35MGFc  Compared with shell-model calculations using the SDPF-M interaction in 
 35MGGc  the sd shell with |n1f{-7/2} and |n2p{-3/2} orbits, and the SDPF-M     
 35MGHc  interaction in a model space up to |n2p{-1/2}, and antisymmetrized     
 35MGIc  molecular dynamics (AMD) model calculations using the Gogny D1S force. 
