 35SI cB $The decay scheme is incomplete due to possible unobserved levels in a 
 35SI2cB large gap of about 6.5 MeV between Q-value=14.17 MeV and the highest   
 35SI3cB populated level at E=7.69 MeV.                                         
 35SI cB IB$For the two bound excited states, I|b{+-} is from the |g+ce         
 35SI2cB intensity balance at each state. Quoted I|b{+-} values without         
 35SI3cB uncertainties are considered upper limits due to the incomplete decay  
 35SI4cB scheme, and the associated log {Ift} values are considered lower       
 35SI5cB limits. For unbound excited states (>2470), I|b{+-} is from the        
 35SI6cB absolute I|b{+-} in 2005Ti11 based on neutron intensities.             
 35SI cB LOGFT$For unbound levels, 2005Ti11 did not report uncertainties for    
 35SI2cB neutron energies or level energies. The evaluators estimate the        
 35SI3cB uncertainties of log {Ift} are <0.1, assuming a 200-keV uncertainty in 
 35SI4cB level energies.                                                        
