 35SI c  {+34}Si(d,p){+35}Si from J|p=0+ {+34}Si g.s. in inverse kinematics.    
 35SI c  2014Bu01: A 20.5-MeV/nucleon, 1.1|*10{+5} pps, and 95% pure {+34}Si    
 35SI2c  secondary beam was produced via the fragmentation of a 55-MeV/nucleon  
 35SI3c  {+36}S{+16+} primary beam impinging on a 1075-|mm-thick Be target,     
 35SI4c  separated by the LISE3 spectrometer at GANIL, and incident on a 2.6-   
 35SI5c  mg/cm{+2} {I1} CD{-2} secondary target. Incoming beam ions were tracked
 35SI6c  using two position-sensitive multiwire proportional chambers upstream  
 35SI7c  of the target. Outgoing ions were identified using an ionization       
 35SI8c  chamber (IC) downstream of target for energy loss and a plastic        
 35SI9c  scintillator behind the IC for TOF measurements. Protons from the (d,p)
 35SIAc  reaction were detected using four modules of the MUST2 array placed 10 
 35SIBc  cm from the target covering polar angles ranging from 105|' to 150|'   
 35SICc  with respect to the beam direction and a 16-strip annular Si detector  
 35SIDc  at a distance of 11.3 cm covering polar angles from 156|' to 168|'. |g 
 35SIEc  rays were detected using four segmented Ge detectors from the EXOGAM   
 35SIFc  array perpendicular to the beam axis at a mean distance of 5 cm, and 9 
 35SIGc  cm downstream from the target with efficiency |e=3.8% {I2} at 1 MeV.   
 35SIHc  Measured |s(E{-p},|q), Doppler-corrected E|g, I|g, ({+34}Si)p-coin.    
 35SIIc  Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfer and spectroscopic factors.           
 35SIJc  Comparisons with shell-model calculations.                             
