 35S     26MG(18O,2ANG)                2021GO09                  ENSDF    202509
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35S  dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 03-Jun-2025)          
 35S  c  2021Go09: {+26}Mg({+18}O,2|an){+35}S fusion-evaporation reaction. Exp 1
 35S 2c  determined the beam energy for producing high-spin states of {+35}S: an
 35S 3c  80-MeV {+18}O beam was delivered from the JAEA tandem accelerator      
 35S 4c  facility and impinged on a 0.5-mg/cm{+2} thick, self-supporting        
 35S 5c  metallic enriched foil of {+26}Mg. |g rays were detected using the     
 35S 6c  GEMINI-II array of 14 Ge detectors with BGO Compton-suppressor shields.
 35S 7c  The reaction channel was selected by detecting the evaporated charged  
 35S 8c  particles with a 4|p silicon detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |a|g|g-coin, 
 35S 9c  |g|g(|q)(ADO). Exp 2 used the same {+18}O beam energy, the same target,
 35S Ac  and the same charged-particle detectors as Exp 1. The beam was         
 35S Bc  delivered from the ALTO-Tandem accelerator facility at IPN Orsay. |g   
 35S Cc  rays were detected using the ORGAM array of 13 Ge detectors based on   
 35S Dc  the EUROGAM array with the BGO scintillator for the anti-Compton       
 35S Ec  suppressor. Compared with large-scale shell-model calculations with the
 35S Fc  SDPF-MSD4 interaction. Also see 2015GoZY, 2014GoZZ, 2013GoZW, and      
 35S Gc  2012IdZZ.                                                              
 35S  cG $R{+|g1}{-ADO}=I|g1(47|' gated by |g{-2} at all angles)/I|g1(86|' gated
 35S 2cG by |g{-2} at all angles). Expected values are |?0.8 for dipole (|DJ=1) 
 35S 3cG and |?1.0 for stretched quadrupole (|DJ=2) transitions.                
