 35S     34S(D,P)                      2024KU24,1971VA18,1969MO12ENSDF    202509
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35S 2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35S  c  J|p=0+ for {+34}S g.s.                                                 
 35S  c  2024Ku24: An 8-MeV/nucleon deuteron beam was produced from the 9-MV    
 35S 2c  Super-FN tandem Van de Graaff accelerator at FSU. The target was       
 35S 3c  carbon-backed sulfur enriched in {+34}S. Protons were spatially        
 35S 4c  dispersed by the Super-Enge Split-Pole Spectrograph and detected using 
 35S 5c  a position-sensitive ionization chamber (|DE) and a plastic            
 35S 6c  scintillator (E) at the focal plane with FWHM|?45 keV. An additional   
 35S 7c  {+34}S(d,p|g){+35}S measurement using the CeBr{-3} Array (CeBrA)       
 35S 8c  demonstrator provides information on some overlapping peaks produced   
 35S 9c  from the {+32}S contaminants in the target. Measured |s(E{-p},|q).     
 35S Ac  Deduced 23 levels, single-neutron spectroscopic factors and strengths  
 35S Bc  from finite-range PTOLEMY-DWBA analysis.                               
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1971Va18: A 10-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the Utrecht 6-MV    
 35S 2c  tandem accelerator. Targets were 100 |mg/cm{+2} PbS on carbon plus     
 35S 3c  formvar foils and 5 |mg/cm{+2} pure {+34}S embedded in aluminum foil.  
 35S 4c  Protons were detected using one 15-mm long and seven 30-mm long, 0.6-mm
 35S 5c  thick position-sensitive detectors (PSD) in the focal plane of the     
 35S 6c  Utrecht split-pole magnetic spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-p},|q).       
 35S 7c  Deduced 17 levels, L-transfers, J, |p, spectroscopic factors from      
 35S 8c  DWUCK-DWBA analysis for the ground state and seven excited states of   
 35S 9c  {+35}S.                                                                
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1969Mo12: A 6.495-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the ONR-CIT      
 35S 2c  tandem accelerator. The target was an enriched target of 450-|mg/cm{+2}
 35S 3c  {I25} CdS (85% {+34}S) evaporated onto a 301-|mg/cm{+2} {I15} gold foil
 35S 4c  and a natural target of 289-|mg/cm{+2} {I30} Sb{+2}S{+3} evaporated    
 35S 5c  onto a 289-|mg/cm{+2} {I30} gold foil. Protons were detected using an  
 35S 6c  array of 16 Au-Si surface barrier detectors with FWHM=30 keV. Measured 
 35S 7c  |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced 37 levels.                                       
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1984Pi03: A 12.3-MeV deuteron beam was produced from a cyclotron. The  
 35S 2c  target was CdS (61.9% in {+36}S, 37.7% in {+34}S), 100 |mg/cm{+2} on a 
 35S 3c  20 |mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Protons were analyzed by a multi-angle   
 35S 4c  magnetic spectrograph and detected using 700-mm long nuclear emulsion  
 35S 5c  plates Ilford L4. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced 13 levels,            
 35S 6c  L-transfers, J, |p, and spectroscopic factors from DWUCK-DWBA analysis 
 35S 7c  for six excited states of {+35}S.                                      
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1979So01: A 3.55-MeV deuteron beam was produced from a Van de Graaff   
 35S 2c  electrostatic generator. The target was 18-|mg/cm{+2} GeS (80% {+36}S, 
 35S 3c  20% {+34}S) on a 25-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Protons were analyzed by
 35S 4c  a magnetic spectrograph and recorded by a spark chamber with FWHM=10-15
 35S 5c  keV. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels.                            
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1971Ko33: A 6.6-MeV deuteron beam was produced from a cyclotron.       
 35S 2c  Targets were GeS films of 70-80 |mg/cm{+2} (98% enrichment in {+34}S)  
 35S 3c  evaporated onto a 20 |mg/cm{+2} carbon substrate. Protons were detected
 35S 4c  using an 800-|mm-thick Si(Li). Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels,  
 35S 5c  J, |p, L-transfers, and spectroscopic factors from distorted-wave      
 35S 6c  analysis for the ground state and five excited states of {+35}S.       
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1971Me12: An 18-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the Yale MP tandem 
 35S 2c  Van de Graaff accelerator. The target was H{+2}S gas of natural        
 35S 3c  isotopic composition (95.06% {+32}S, 4.18% {+34}S). Protons were       
 35S 4c  detected using a |DE-E telescope of silicon surface-barrier detectors. 
 35S 5c  Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, and         
 35S 6c  spectroscopic factors from local, zero-range JULIE-DWBA analysis of    
 35S 7c  |s(E{-p},|q) for the ground state and two excited states of {+35}S.    
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1966Sc09: 9- and 12-MeV deuteron beams were produced from the Argonne  
 35S 2c  tandem accelerator. The target was PbS. Protons were detected using    
 35S 3c  silicon surface barrier detectors. Measured |s(E{-p},|q) for the ground
 35S 4c  state and one excited state of {+35}S.                                 
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  1958En51: 6.006- and 6.542-MeV deuteron beams were produced from the   
 35S 2c  MIT-ONR electrostatic generator. Targets were Sb{+2}S{+3} of natural   
 35S 3c  isotopic constitution (4.2% {+34}S). Energies of charged reaction      
 35S 4c  products emitted from the target at angles of 50, 90, and 130|' were   
 35S 5c  measured by a broad-range magnetic spectrograph and nuclear emulsions. 
 35S 6c  Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced 5 levels.                               
 35S  d                                                                         
 35S  c  Other measurements: 1976We29: {+34}S(d,p){+35}S angular distributions  
 35S 2c  for the ground state and the first excited state of {+35}S. 1973Co25:  
 35S 3c  {+34}S(d,p){+35}S excitation functions for the two lowest excited      
 35S 4c  states of {+35}S.                                                      
 35S  c  Theoretical calculations: 1977Os07, 1974Os02.                          
