 35S  c  1971Vi02: A 40-MeV proton beam was produced from the Grenoble variable 
 35S 2c  energy cyclotron at intensities of 20-200 nA depending on the          
 35S 3c  scattering angle with a 90-keV energy resolution. The target was       
 35S 4c  natural purified chlorine gas 100 mm in diameter and 25 mm in height.  
 35S 5c  The reaction particles were detected using two separate counter        
 35S 6c  telescopes with each consisting of a 200-|mm phosphorous-drifted       
 35S 7c  silicon |DE detector, a 2-mm lithium-drifted silicon E detector and a  
 35S 8c  3-mm lithium-drifted silicon E-reject detector with FWHM=180 keV for   
 35S 9c  {+3}He. Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced L for {+35}S ground state   
 35S Ac  from zero-range Nelson spin-dependent-DWBA analysis of the measured    
 35S Bc  |s(|q).                                                                
