 35S  c  1975VaYG,1972Va07: A 4.25-MeV deuteron beam of 55 nA was provided from 
 35S 2c  the Groningen 5 MV Van de Graaff generator. The target was 100         
 35S 3c  |mg/cm{+2} Co{+37}Cl enriched to 98% evaporated onto 10-|mg/cm{+2}     
 35S 4c  Formvar plus 10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon. |a particles were detected using a  
 35S 5c  60-|mm annular silicon detector. |g rays were detected using a 120     
 35S 6c  cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector at 90|'. Measured |s(E{-|a}), E|g, I|g, and     
 35S 7c  |a|g-coin. Deduced levels, |g-ray branching ratios. Also see 1971VaZG. 
 35S  c  1968Te06: 3.1-4.6-MeV deuteron beams of 50 nA were provided from the   
 35S 2c  Groningen 5-MV Van de Graaff generator. The target was a 100-|mg/cm{+2}
 35S 3c  Co{+37}Cl both of natural {+37}Cl abundance and enriched to 93%        
 35S 4c  evaporated onto 10-|mg/cm{+2} Formvar plus 10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon. |a    
 35S 5c  particles were detected using an annular solid-state detector at       
 35S 6c  168-173|'. |g rays were detected using a 3 in. by 3 in. NaI(Tl)        
 35S 7c  scintillator at 55|'. Measured |s(E{-|a}), E|g, and |a|g-coin. Deduced 
 35S 8c  levels.                                                                
 35S  c  1955Pa54: {+37}Cl(d,|a){+35}S with 3.0, 5.6, 6.0, 7.0, and 7.5-MeV     
 35S 2c  deuteron beams from the MIT-ONR electrostatic generator. Targets were  
 35S 3c  80 and 300-|mg/cm{+2} barium chloride (75.4% {+35}Cl, 24.6% {+37}Cl)   
 35S 4c  evaporated onto Formvar films on a gold layer. Charged reaction        
 35S 5c  products emitted at 90|' were magnetically analyzed by a broad-range   
 35S 6c  spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-|a}). Deduced levels.                     
