 35CL3cDP Proton decay is assumed to populate only the ground state of the      
 35CL4cDP daughter nucleus {+35}Cl based on the arguments proposed in 1996Il02: 
 35CL5cDP (A) unreasonably small log {Ift} values if populating excited states; 
 35CL6cDP (B) no pairs of particle groups characteristic of the g.s./first      
 35CL7cDP excited state energy difference; (C) compatible level matching with   
 35CL8cDP resonance reaction studies.                                           
