 35CL c  {+31}P+|a|){+35}Cl from J|p=1/2+ {+31}P ground state.                  
 35CL c  1979Es05,1978Es01: a 36-MeV {+6}Li{+3+} beam at 150-400 nA was produced
 35CL2c  from the MP tandem accelerator at the University of Rochester and      
 35CL3c  bombarded a 100-|mg/cm{+2}cadmium phosphide Cd{-3}P{-2} target.        
 35CL4c  Outgoing deuterons were momentum analyzed by an Enge split-pole        
 35CL5c  magnetic spectrograph and detected using Kodak NTB-50 nuclear emulsion 
 35CL6c  plates with FWHM=50 keV. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, 
 35CL7c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from finite-range, LOLA-DWBA        
 35CL8c  analysis of the measured |s(|q).                                       
 35CL c  Other: 1982Ch10 (finite-range DWBA calculations).                      
 35CL cL $Spectroscopic factor g*S=|s(|q){-exp}/|s(|q){-DWBA}, where            
 35CL2cL g=(2J{-f}+1)/(2J{-i}+1)                                                
