 35CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 19-Aug-2025)          
 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+32}S ground state.                                        
 35CL c  1970Ho09: 10.975-, 11.960-, 12.120-MeV |a beams were produced from the 
 35CL2c  Chalk River MP tandem accelerator. Targets were 100-|mg/cm{+2}         
 35CL3c  Sb{-2}S{-3} on a 10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. |g rays were detected   
 35CL4c  using 15.2-cm-long by 12.7-cm-diam NaI(Tl) detectors. Protons were     
 35CL5c  detected using an annular silicon surface barrier detector close to    
 35CL6c  180|' with FWHM=30 keV for protons and FWHM=50 keV for |a. Measured    
 35CL7c  E{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g(|q). Deduced 25 level energies from E{-p}, J,     
 35CL8c  branching ratios, multipole mixing ratios.                             
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1972Br33: a 10-MeV |a beam was produced from the Chalk River MP tandem 
 35CL2c  accelerator. Targets were 340-|mg/cm{+2} Sb{-2}S{-3} on gold backings. 
 35CL3c  |g rays were detected using a 44-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector inside an      
 35CL4c  anticoincidence split annular NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E|g, I|g.     
 35CL5c  Deduced 11 level energies, 16 |g branching ratios, 11 lifetimes using  
 35CL6c  the Doppler Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM). 1970In01 from the same    
 35CL7c  experiment deduced the lifetime using DSAM for a level at 3942 keV and 
 35CL8c  the mixing ratio for a 3942|)2646 |g transition.                       
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973Al22: a 14-MeV |a beam was produced from the 80-cm cyclotron at the
 35CL2c  Research Institute for Physics in Stockholm and 12-16-MeV |a beams were
 35CL3c  produced from the Uppsala tandem accelerator. Targets were prepared by 
 35CL4c  depositing pulverized sulphur enriched to 99.9% in {+32}S on lead      
 35CL5c  backings. |g rays were detected using an Ortec 60-cm{+3} Ge(Li)        
 35CL6c  detector with FWHM=2.2 keV at 1333 keV and an additional Canberra      
 35CL7c  60-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector for |g|g-coincidence measurements. Measured  
 35CL8c  E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q) for 4 |g rays. Deduced 12 level energies   
 35CL9c  from E|g, J for 4 levels, branching ratios, and mixing ratios.         
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1969In04: 6-8-MeV |a beams were produced from the Chalk River MP tandem
 35CL2c  accelerator. A thick target (270 |mg/cm{+2}) of natural sulfur on a    
 35CL3c  tantalum backing and a thin target (50 |mg/cm{+2}) of Sb{-2}S{-3} on a 
 35CL4c  gold backing were used. |g rays were detected using two Ge(Li)         
 35CL5c  detectors of 15 and 40 cm{+3} volume. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced 6     
 35CL6c  level energies, branching ratios, 5 lifetimes using the Doppler Shift  
 35CL7c  Attenuation Method (DSAM) and 1 lifetime for the 3163-keV level using  
 35CL8c  the Recoil Distance Method (RDM), and transition strengths.            
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1974Lo17: 11.0, 12.0 and 14.7-MeV |a beams were produced from the      
 35CL2c  Oliver Lodge Laboratory at the University of Liverpool. Targets were   
 35CL3c  natural CdS. Protons were detected using an annular |DE-E telescope    
 35CL4c  close to 180|' with FWHM=80 keV. |g rays were detected using five      
 35CL5c  NaI(Tl) detectors and one Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g, p|g-coin,
 35CL6c  p|g(|q), |g|g-coin, |g-ray linear polarization. Deduced J and |p for 3 
 35CL7c  levels, 6 |g branching ratios, 5 mixing ratios, and lifetimes for a    
 35CL8c  5408-keV level using DSAM and for a 6088-keV level using RDM.          
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973Br26: a 11.2-MeV |a beam was produced from the Legnaro (Padova) Van
 35CL2c  de Graaff generator. Targets were natural CdS. |g rays were detected   
 35CL3c  using a Ge(Li) detector. Deduced the lifetime using the Recoil Distance
 35CL4c  Method (RDM) for a level at 3163 keV.                                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973An01: 5.5- and 8.6-MeV |a beams of 100-200 nA were produced from   
 35CL2c  the Oxford Vertical Van de Graaff (Injector) or the Oxford EN Tandem.  
 35CL3c  Targets were natural sulphur in AgS. |g rays were detected using a     
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector at 0|'. Deduced the lifetime using the Recoil Distance 
 35CL5c  Method (RDM) for a level at 3163 keV.                                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL cG E$Values with uncertainties are from 1973Al22 and those without        
 35CL2cG uncertainties are from level-energy differences, unless otherwise      
 35CL3cG noted. 1973Al22 is the only literature in this dataset that reported   
 35CL4cG measured E|g with uncertainties. 1969In04 and 1972Br33 reported        
 35CL5cG E(level) with uncertainties derived from their measured E|g but did not
 35CL6cG report E|g. Evaluators adopt the uncertainties of E(level) from        
 35CL7cG 1969In04 and 1972Br33 as the uncertainties of an E|g if this |g        
 35CL8cG transition populates the ground state and is also the dominant decay   
 35CL9cG branch of that level.                                                  
 35CL cG RI$From 1969In04 for |g rays from level up to 3163, from 1972Br33 for  
 35CL2cG |g rays from level above 3163 up to 4618 level, and from 1974Lo17 for  
 35CL3cG |g rays from level above 4618, unless otherwise noted                  
 35CL cG M,MR$Mult=D+Q, Q or Q+O and |d are determined from p|g(|q) in 1970Ho09;
 35CL2cG magnetic or electric characters are determined based on RUL and        
 35CL3cG measured level T{-1/2} where available, unless otherwise noted         
 35CL cL E$From a least-squares fit to E|g values with uncertainties, unless    
 35CL2cL otherwise noted.                                                       
 35CL cL J$Spin assignments are from p|g(|q) in 1970Ho09, unless otherwise noted
 35CL cL E(Y)$From 1970Ho09, derived from measured E{-p}.                       
