 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+34}S ground state.                                        
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1976Me12: 0.7-2.1-MeV proton beams were produced from the 1.1-MV       
 35CL2c  Cockroft-Walton generator and a 3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets
 35CL3c  were ZnS (46% {+34}S) and CdS (37% {+34}S) on tantalum backings. |g    
 35CL4c  rays were detected using a 10-cm by 10-cm NaI detector and a 40-cm{+3} 
 35CL5c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, |g(|q). Deduced level        
 35CL6c  energies for 33 bound states and 47 resonances, J, |p, resonance       
 35CL7c  strengths, |g branching ratios, mixing ratios, and lifetimes for 25    
 35CL8c  bound states using DSAM.                                               
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1976Sp08: 1.21,1.95-2.91-MeV protons were produced from the Utrecht    
 35CL2c  University 3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were Ag{+2}S (95%   
 35CL3c  {+34}) evaporated onto a tantalum backing. |g rays were detected using 
 35CL4c  a 10 cm by 10 cm diameter NaI scintillator and a 120- or 60-cm{+3}     
 35CL5c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured reaction yields, E|g. Deduced Q value, 84    
 35CL6c  resonance energies, resonance strengths, widths, J, |p, and            
 35CL7c  |g-branching ratios.                                                   
 35CL c  1976Sp09: similar setup as 1976Sp08 with 2.33-2.79-MeV protons.        
 35CL2c  Measured reaction yields, E|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, and      
 35CL3c  |g-branching ratios.                                                   
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1972Hu10: 0.7-2.1-MeV protons were produced from the 4-MV Van de Graaff
 35CL2c  at the Centre d'Etudes Nucleaires de Bordeaux-Gradignan. Targets were  
 35CL3c  100-|mg/cm{+2} Ag{-2}S (90% {+34}S). |g rays were detected using a     
 35CL4c  12.7-cm by 12.7-cm NaI(Tl) detector and a 60-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector.   
 35CL5c  Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, I|g. Deduced 59 resonances, 32 bound states,  
 35CL6c  resonance strengths, and |g branching ratios.                          
 35CL c  1972Hu11: similar setup as 1972Hu10. Deduced lifetimes using DSAM.     
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973Fa07: 1-2-MeV protons were produced from the Helsinki 2-MV Van de  
 35CL2c  Graaff accelerator. Targets were {+34}S on tantalum backings. |g rays  
 35CL3c  were detected using a 55-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector. Measured reaction     
 35CL4c  yields, E|g, I|g. Deduced 28 resonances, resonance strengths,          
 35CL5c  |g-branching ratios, and 9 lifetimes using DSAM.                       
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  2001Vo24: 1.183-2.820-MeV protons were produced from the 4-MeV         
 35CL2c  electrostatic Van de Graaff accelerator (NSC KhPEI). Enriched {+34}S   
 35CL3c  target (100%). A 63 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector and a 15-cm-diam by         
 35CL4c  10-cm-long NaI(Tl) detector. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, I|g. Deduced 12  
 35CL5c  resonances and resonance strengths.                                    
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  2002Vo17: 2.187-MeV protons were produced from the ESU-4 accelerator   
 35CL2c  (NSC KhPEI). Enriched {+34}S target. A 63 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector.      
 35CL3c  Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, resonance strengths, widths.        
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1981Bi05: 1.4-2.8-MeV protons were produced from the Groningen 5-MV Van
 35CL2c  de Graaff accelerator. Targets were 4 and 1-|mg/cm{+2} Sb{-2}S{-3} (90%
 35CL3c  in {+34}S) evaporated onto 10-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backings. Scattered    
 35CL4c  protons were detected using three silicon surface barrier detectors. |g
 35CL5c  rays were detected using a 10-cm by 10-cm NaI(Tl) detector and a Ge(Li)
 35CL6c  detector. Measured |s(E{-p},|q), E|g, |g(|q) for two |g rays. Deduced  
 35CL7c  levels, J, |p, widths, and resonance strengths.                        
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1971Wi13: protons were produced from the Ontario Cancer Institute.     
 35CL2c  Targets were CdS. |g rays were detected using NaI(Tl) and Ge(Li)       
 35CL3c  detectors. Measured |s(E{-p}),E|g, I|g, |g(|q), |g-linear polarization.
 35CL4c  Deduced 1.020-, 1.214-, 1.267-, and 1.510-MeV resonances, J|p,         
 35CL5c  branchings, mixing ratios, and half-lives using DSAM.                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1971Pr11: 1.211-MeV protons were produced from the 2-MeV ARL Van de    
 35CL2c  Graaff at the Aerospace Research Laboratories (ARL). Targets were      
 35CL3c  Ag{-2}S (85.6% {+34}S). |g rays were detected using an 80-cm{+3} Ge(Li)
 35CL4c  detector. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, I|g, |g(|q), p|g-delay. Deduced     
 35CL5c  resonances, levels, J, |p, branchings.                                 
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1963Ha32: 0.7-1.2-MeV protons were produced from the Laboratorium      
 35CL2c  Technische Fysika. Target was {+34}S. |g rays were detected using      
 35CL3c  NaI(TI) scintillation spectrometers. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, I|g.     
 35CL4c  Deduced levels, branchings.                                            
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1967Da12: 0.8-2.5-MeV protons were produced from the 2.5 MeV Van de    
 35CL2c  Graaff generator of the U.A.R. Atomic Energy Establishment. Targets    
 35CL3c  were {+34}S on tantalum backings. |g rays were detected using two      
 35CL4c  15.2-cm-diam by 12.7-cm-thick NaI(Tl) crystals. Measured |s(E{-p}),    
 35CL5c  E|g, I|g. Deduced resonances, levels, branchings.                      
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1960An06: 0.7-1.9-MeV protons were produced from the electrostatic     
 35CL2c  generator of the Physical-Technical Institute of the Ukrainian SSR     
 35CL3c  Academy of Sciences. Targets were isotopic {+34}S (4.2%). |g rays were 
 35CL4c  detected using a 2-cm-thick by 3-cm-diam CsI(Tl) crystal. Measured     
 35CL5c  |s(E{-p}), E|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, branchings.                 
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1966Wa09: 1.214 MeV proton beam. Measured E|g, |g-polarization. Deduced
 35CL2c  level energy and J, |p for the level of 3163 and 7540 level.           
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1966En04: 0.3-2.1-MeV protons were produced from the Utrecht 850-keV   
 35CL2c  Cockcroft-Walton generator and the 3-MV Van de Graaff generator.       
 35CL3c  Targets were natural sulphur compound on tantalum backings. |g rays    
 35CL4c  were detected using a cylindrical 10-cm-by-10-cm NaI crystal. Measured 
 35CL5c  |s(E{-p}), E|g. Deduced the resonance strength for E{-p}=1214 keV.     
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1966Az01: 1.214-MeV protons were produced from the Ontario Cancer      
 35CL2c  Institute 3-MeV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were CdS with       
 35CL3c  enriched {+34}S (46%). |g rays were detected using a Compton           
 35CL4c  polarimeter. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,         
 35CL5c  branchings.                                                            
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1967Wa22: 1.214- and 1.512-MeV protons were produced from the Aerospace
 35CL2c  Research Laboratories. Targets were enriched CdS (40% {+34}S) and      
 35CL3c  Ag{-2}S (86% {+34}S). |g rays were detected using two large volume     
 35CL4c  NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, I|g, |g(|q),               
 35CL5c  |g-polarization. Deduced levels, J, |p, branchings.                    
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1967Ta08: 1.020-, 1.213- and 1.513-MeV protons were produced from the  
 35CL2c  3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator of the Ontario Cancer Institute. Targets
 35CL3c  were CdS (46% {+34}S) on thick metal foils. |g rays were detected using
 35CL4c  a 7.6-cm-long by 7.6-cm-diam NaI(Tl) detector. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g,
 35CL5c  I|g, |g(|q), |g-polarization. Deduced levels, J, |p, branchings, mixing
