 35CL c  1969Da12: a 4.95-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the 5.5-MeV Van de
 35CL2c  Graaff accelerator at University of Alberta and impinged on a CdS      
 35CL3c  target enriched to 37% {+34}S evaporated onto a 0.05-cm gold backing.  
 35CL4c  Neutrons were detected by NE213 scintillators using the time-of-flight 
 35CL5c  (tof) method with FWHM=1.0 ns. Measured |s(E{-n},|q). Deduced levels,  
 35CL6c  J, |p, and L-transfers from DWUCK-DWBA analysis of the measured |s(|q).
 35CL c  1993TeZX: {+34}S(d,n){+35}Cl at E(d)=25 MeV at CYRJC, Tohoku           
 35CL2c  University.                                                            
