 35CL c  1984El12,1989Ge09: fast neutrons of diameter 26 mm were produced from  
 35CL2c  the IRT-2000 reactor at the Institute for Nuclear Research and Nuclear 
 35CL3c  Power of the Bulgarian Academy of Sciences in Sofia. Two {+35}Cl       
 35CL4c  targets were placed at 45|' and 135|' with a distance of 70 cm apart.  
 35CL5c  |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g. Deduced   
 35CL6c  lifetimes for 4 levels using the Doppler Shift Attenuation Method      
 35CL7c  (DSAM) and transition strengths.                                       
 35CL c  1966Ni03: 2.5-4.2-MeV neutrons were produced via the T(p,n) reactions  
 35CL2c  with protons from the university of Kentucky 6-MeV accelerator. Targets
 35CL3c  were a cylinder of CCl{-4} and a 5.6-cm-diam sphere of C{-2}Cl{-6}. |g 
 35CL4c  rays were detected using a 6.35-cm by 6.35-cm NaI(Tl) detector and     
 35CL5c  7.5-cc Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J   
 35CL c  1971Fr05: neutrons up to 10 MeV were produced from a 5-Ci Pu-Be neutron
 35CL2c  source and bombarded table salt targets. |g rays were detected using a 
 35CL3c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured 2 |g rays and deduced 2 levels.              
