 35AR c  2007De14,2005DeZZ: A 70-MeV {+16}O beam was produced by the XTU-Tandem 
 35AR2c  accelerator at the Legnaro National Laboratory, Italy. The target was a
 35AR3c  400 |mg/cm{+2} self-supporting target of {+24}Mg. |g ray from fusion   
 35AR4c  evaporation reactions of {+24}Mg({+16}O,|an|g){+35}Ar and              
 35AR5c  {+24}Mg({+16}O,|ap|g){+35}Cl were detected using the GASP spectrometer,
 35AR6c  which consists of an array of 40 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors and 
 35AR7c  a multiplicity filter of 80 BGO scintillators. The GASP spectrometer is
 35AR8c  operated in conjunction with the 4|p charged-particle detector ISIS and
 35AR9c  a neutron ring of 6 BC501A scintillators. The events were collected    
 35ARAc  when at least two Ge detectors and one BGO scintillator were fired in  
 35ARBc  coincidence. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |an|g-coin, |ap|g-coin, |g(|q),  
 35ARCc  |g|g(|q)(ADO). Deduced levels, J, |p, and transition multipolarities   
 35ARDc  from |g-ray ADO ratios. Comparisons with Shell-model calculations show 
 35AREc  the multipole Coulomb interaction and the electromagnetic spin-orbit   
 35ARFc  interaction contribute to the observed mirror energy differences.      
 35ARGc  2007De14 also report data on {+35}Cl and propose the level scheme of   
 35ARHc  {+35}Ar based on mirror symmetry                                       
 35AR cG $R{-ADO}=[I|g(34|')+I|g(146|')]/2I|g(90|'). Expected values are        
