 35K  dE EAV,LOGFT$FROM BetaShape v2.4 (Jun-2024) 2023Mo21.                     
 35K  c  1999Tr04, 1998Le45: A secondary {+35}Ca beam at 0.3 ions/s and 98%     
 35K 2c  purity was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a              
 35K 3c  95-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca{+20+} primary beam impinging on a rotating      
 35K 4c  {+nat}Ni target, selected using |DE-ToF by the GANIL LISE3             
 35K 5c  spectrometer, and implanted into a 500-|mm thick silicon detector      
 35K 6c  sandwiched between two 500-|mm thick silicon detectors for detecting   
 35K 7c  |b{++} particles. 3.5|*10{+4} {+35}Ca ions were stopped at a depth of  
 35K 8c  300 |mm with FWHM=70 |mm (setting 1) and 2.5|*10{+4} {+35}Ca ions were 
 35K 9c  stopped at a depth of 450 |mm (setting 2). |e+|b{++}-delayed protons   
 35K Ac  were detected by the implantation detector. |g rays were detected by   
 35K Bc  three Ge detectors and two NaI detectors. Measured E{-p}, I{-p}, E|g,  
 35K Cc  I|g, E{-2p}, I{-2p}, |bp-coin, p|g-coin. Built the decay scheme        
 35K Dc  consisting of 1p-emitting states in {+35}K, a 2p-emitting state (T=5/2 
 35K Ec  IAS) in {+35}K, 1p daughter states in {+34}Ar, and a 2p daughter state 
 35K Fc  in {+33}Cl. Deduced decay branching ratios, B(GT) and B(F), and parent 
 35K Gc  {+35}Ca T{-1/2} from implant-decay correlations.                       
 35K  d                                                                         
 35K  c  1985Ay01: {+35}Ca isotope discovery. {+35}Ca was produced by bombarding
 35K 2c  a natural calcium target using a 135-MeV {+3}He beam from the 88-inch  
 35K 3c  Cyclotron at Lawrence Berkeley Laboratory. Recoiling products were     
 35K 4c  slowed down, transported, and collected on a slowly rotating catcher   
 35K 5c  wheel. The |e+|b{++}-delayed protons were detected using Si detector   
 35K 6c  telescopes. Measured E{-p}, I{-p}, pp-coin. Built the decay scheme     
 35K 7c  consisting of a 2p-emitting state (T=5/2 IAS) in {+35}K, sequential 2p 
 35K 8c  intermediate states in {+34}Ar, and 2p daughter states in {+33}Cl.     
 35K 9c  Deduced {+35}Ca T{-1/2} and {+35}Ca mass using the known members of    
 35K Ac  A=35, T=5/2 sextuplets IMME.                                           
 35K  c  Theoretical studies involving {+35}Ca decay: 2003Sm02, 1991De26,       
 35K 2c  1990Br26                                                               
 35K  c  The decay scheme is considered relatively complete as all observed     
 35K 2c  individual I(1p) and I(2p) add up to almost 100% in 1999Tr04.          
 35K  cL E$Evaluators deduced E(level)({+35}K)=E(p){-lab}|*[m(p)+m({+34}Ar)]/m(\
 35K 2cL {+34}Ar)+S(p)({+35}K)+E(level)({+34}Ar), with S(p)({+35}K)=83.6 {I5}   
 35K 3cL (2021Wa16), E(level)({+34}Ar) from 2012Ni10, and E(p){-lab} from       
 35K 4cL 1999Tr04. For a {+35}K proton-emitting level with multiple proton      
 35K 5cL branches, evaluators take the weighted average for E(level)({+35}K)    
 35K 6cL values deduced from each proton branch. 1999Tr04 used S(p)({+35}K)=78  
 35K 7cL {I20} from 1993Au07, which causes a small difference between the       
 35K 8cL original E(level)({+35}K) in 1999Tr04 and the deduced E(level)({+35}K) 
 35K 9cL here.                                                                  
