 35K  cE TI$Deduced from the I(p) values in 1999Tr04 multiplied by 0.994. The   
 35K 2cE original %|SI(1p)=96.4 {I18} and %|SI(2p)=4.2 {I3} in 1999Tr04 lead to 
 35K 3cE %|SI(1p)+%|SI(2p)=100.6. The evaluators perform a renormalization of   
 35K 4cE 100.6 to 100, which yields the factor of 0.994. The original I(p) in   
 35K 5cE 1999Tr04 was determined from the number of observed proton events and  
 35K 6cE the total number of implants, with simulated proton-detection          
 35K 7cE efficiencies.                                                          
