 35K  c  1976Be08: {+35}K isotope discovery. {+40}Ca({+3}He,{+8}Li){+35}K is    
 35K 2c  studied using 73.7- and 75.8-MeV {+3}He beams produced by the Michigan 
 35K 3c  State University cyclotron. Targets were 370 and 190 |mg/cm{+2}        
 35K 4c  enriched {+40}Ca on a 20 |mg/cm{+2} natural carbon backing. {+8}Li     
 35K 5c  particles were detected using a scintillator-proportional counter      
 35K 6c  detector system at the focal plane of the Enge split-pole spectrograph.
