 35CA c  J|p=3/2+ for {+37}Ca ground state.                                     
 35CA c  2023La09: A 50-MeV/nucleon {+37}Ca secondary beam was produced via the 
 35CA2c  fragmentation of a 95-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca{+20+} primary beam impinging 
 35CA3c  on a {+9}Be target, selected by the LISE3 spectrometer at GANIL, and   
 35CA4c  then impinged on a liquid hydrogen cryogenic target (CRYPTA). Beam ions
 35CA5c  before target were tracked using two low-pressure multiwire            
 35CA6c  proportional chambers (CATS). Heavy residuals after target were        
 35CA7c  detected by a zero-degree detection system consisting of an ionization 
 35CA8c  chamber, a set of two XY drift chambers, and a plastic scintillator.   
 35CA9c  Tritons from 2n-transfer were detected using a set of six MUST2        
 35CAAc  DSSD-CsI telescopes in coincidence with the heavy residues of Ca or Ar.
 35CABc  Measured |s(E{-t},|q) in inverse kinematics. Deduced levels, J, |p,    
 35CACc  L-transfers from FRESCO-DWBA analysis of measured |s(|q).              
 35CA c  First measurement of {+35}Ca mass excess: 4777 keV {I105}.             
 35CA c  First observation of excited states in {+35}Ca.                        
 35CA c  Evidence of the magicity of N=16 close to the proton drip line.        
 35CA d  Also see Louis Lalann, Ph.D. thesis, Paris-Saclay University, France,  
 35CA2d  2021. https://theses.hal.science/tel-03414417v1                        
